diff --git a/source/defining-extensions.html b/source/defining-extensions.html
index 4b559f9a5d..37eef6527a 100644
--- a/source/defining-extensions.html
+++ b/source/defining-extensions.html
@@ -108,7 +108,8 @@ Extensions SHALL only be used on a target that appears in their context list.
     Element values include specialization logic; e.g. if the context of an extension is <code>Element</code>, then 
     this includes all specializations of element, and if the context of an extension is <code>DomainResource.meta</code>,
     the extension can be used in meta for all specializations of DomainResource. The same logic applies to interfaces like 
-    <code>CanonicalResource</code> - these are valid contexts.
+    <code>CanonicalResource</code> - these are valid contexts. If the context identifies a path defined on an interface,
+    the extension can only be used on implementing resources that have that path.
   </li>
   <li>
     <code>Resource</code> is also a valid context, though not all specializations of Resource allow extensions on the root, and the extension can't be used with those resources.
