diff --git a/source/structuredefinition/structuredefinition-notes.xml b/source/structuredefinition/structuredefinition-notes.xml
index e4cab985c2..af99f0cdd7 100644
--- a/source/structuredefinition/structuredefinition-notes.xml
+++ b/source/structuredefinition/structuredefinition-notes.xml
@@ -188,6 +188,9 @@ This list shows a number of examples, with links to real examples for each:
 On this list, structure definitions of type 1, 3, 5 and 8 - 9 can only be defined by the FHIR specification itself. The other kinds of structure definitions
 are (or may be) created by the specification but can also be defined by other implementers.
 </p>
+<p>
+Constraints declared on an interface apply to resources that implement the interface wherever the corresponding element is present. Snapshot generation propagates those inherited constraints into the implementing resource or profile and preserves the interface as the <code>ElementDefinition.constraint.source</code>. If an implementing resource does not have the element path constrained by the interface, that constraint has no matching element on which to apply.
+</p>
 
